        {
          "id": "098a28aa-6c9d-34d6-83a9-1ccdd06ba38b",
          "content": {
            "id": "098a28aa-6c9d-34d6-83a9-1ccdd06ba38b",
            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "U.S. 10-Year Treasury Yield Jumps to Highest Level Since Early Sept",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "The 10-year U.S. Treasury yield rose to 4.275% in early trade, the highest level since early September, according to Tradeweb data.  The rise comes amid U.S. President Trump's latest tariff threats on several European countries over his plan to acquire Greenland.  \"If the dispute over Greenland continues to escalate, it is quite possible that EU investors will sell off U.S. government bonds,\" BlueBay's Kaspar Hense said in a note.",
